{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-12",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Three reference locations defining an open epsilon neighborhood of a. Filled reference markers do not mean that the two boundary locations belong to the open interval. Coordinate spacing is a modern regularization of the epsilon offsets, not an optical measurement.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/9c/figures/fig-12.png",
      "sha256": "146c1be8f0219c511009d5c3d7d538ec9e2ee0d79be2cd7baffd0a8b0437ec37"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "ana9-c3-s2-n21",
        "text": "我们来阐明数列的极限的几何意义. 不等式 (2) 等价于双不等式$-\\varepsilon<x_n-a<\\varepsilon$，或者$a-\\varepsilon<x_n<a+\\varepsilon$. (3)"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "ana9-c3-s2-n21",
        "text": "不等式(3)说明，收敛于$a$的数列$(x_n)$中，所有序号$n>N$的项，即$x_{N+1}$，$x_{N+2}$，…，均落到开区间$]a-\\varepsilon,a+\\varepsilon[$内(图12).这个区间叫做点$a$的$\\varepsilon$邻域."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "ana9-c3-s2-n21",
        "text": "因此，如果数$a$是数列$(x_n)$的极限，那么该数列的项，除了有限项外，全都落到点$a$的任意一个（不管怎样小的）邻域内."
      }
    ],
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "three-reference-locations",
        "description": "Source pixels show exactly three filled collinear marks labelled below, left to right a minus epsilon, a, a plus epsilon. No x_n, zero, ticks, bracket marks, endpoint circles or shaded interval. Unit coordinate offsets are modern regularization justified by the labels, not measured source distances.",
        "objects": ["left-boundary", "limit", "right-boundary"],
        "assertions": ["three-points", "left-order", "right-order", "reference-collinearity"],
        "requires": ["pointRelationships"]
      },
      {
        "id": "right-directed-ungraduated-line",
        "description": "One horizontal stroke extends beyond both outer reference marks, with an unmarked left terminal and a right arrowhead. Neither terminal is a neighborhood boundary. The separate Chinese figure caption is not baked into the diagram.",
        "objects": ["number-line"],
        "assertions": ["directed-line", "one-arrow"]
      }
    ]
  },
